<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada may buy more bonds, fewer T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada may buy more bonds, fewer T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada on Wednesday said it may increase the pace of its bond purchases in order to reduce its participation in treasury bill tenders even further.</p>
<p>The central bank said one possibility under consideration is its acquisition at auction, beginning in November, of 15 percent of bonds maturing beyond the three-year benchmark.</p>
</text>
